      "writtenOn": "2021-01-22T14:15:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is read from one source (ConnectivityService), while the signal to show the notification comes from another (NetworkMonitor). Technically that\u0027s racy: between the time that NetworkMonitor decided to show a portal, and the time this was updated, the NetworkAgentInfo may have changed.\n\nIdeally this should be added to INetworkMonitorCallbacks.showProvisioningNotification, with something like INetworkMonitorCallback#showProvisioningNotificationWithExtra(android.net.networkstack.aidl.ProvisioningNotificationInfo)\n\nThat said updating the AIDL interface and maintaining the two endpoints is expensive, so considering that the network agent data should be available at that point and shouldn\u0027t change with the current use-cases, maybe we can live with this...\nMaybe at least add a comment to explain the tradeoff.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2860,
        "startChar": 62,
        "endLine": 2860,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "c8d4ec1fbfb3bcc68c500a36c40133a6090d6314",
